<?xml version="1.0"?>
<CP_Scriptfile date="Feb 20, 2023">
<CPscript title="Constant Degree Packings" level="min" >
<description>We consider constant degree circle packings, those in which every circle has the same number n of neighbors. We consider degrees n = 6, n = 7, and finally n = 5. Our interest is in the effect that n has on geometry.</description>
<text> We first build constant degree 6 and 7 complexes in side-by-side windows. Begin with simple flowers, add a new generations to each by pressing 'g'. Watch the action. (Caution: the 7-degree pattern grows very (!!) rapidly, so don't  press 'g' too often.) </text>
<cmd name="*" mnemonic="*" tooltip="Start over" iconname="centrejust.png">act 0;Cleanse;Map 0 1;seed 6;max_pack;disp -w -c;seed -p1 7;max_pack -p1;disp -p1 -w -c; </cmd>
<cmd name="g" mnemonic="g" tooltip="add a generation of boundary vertices" iconname="dnd_multi.png">act 0;add_gen 1 6;max_pack;disp -c;add_gen -p1 1 7;max_pack -p1;disp -p1 -c; </cmd>
<text> The next command cleans up the images. Before you do that, note the difference in character between the two cases after a few 'g' operations --- in particular, note the sizes of the circles at the origin. The 'n' command renormalizes the 6-degree so the circle at the origin has the same euclidean size as it does in p1. </text>
<cmd name="c" mnemonic="c" tooltip="show clean 6/7 results" iconname="kuickshow.png">disp -p0 -w -c;disp -p1 -w -c; </cmd>
<cmd name="n" mnemonic="n" tooltip="Renormalize the 6 degree packing" iconname="mozilla.png">geom_to_e -p0;norm_scale -p0 -c 1 .26;disp -p0 -w -c -cf 1;disp -p1 -cf 1 </cmd>
<text> I hope you get some insight into why the infinite 6-degree packing is "flat" (euclidean), while the infinite 7-degree is hyperbolic. Modify the commands to try your hand at an 8 or 9-degree example. </text>
<Section title="The Degree 5 case">
<text> The degree 5 case is entirely different. Think it through for yourself first, then try these commands. </text>
<cmd tooltip="the degree 5 starts with a 6-flower." iconname="psi.png">act 2;Map -x;seed 5;max_pack;Disp -w -cfc207; </cmd>
<cmd iconname="xeyes.png">act 2;add_gen 1 5;max_pack;disp -wr; </cmd>
<cmd iconname="kivio.png">act 2;proj;NSpole;disp -wr </cmd>
</Section>
  </CPscript>
